## Leaf rules

- Never revert a change you did not make; no `git commit`, `stash`, `checkout`, `reset` or `restore`.
- Edit only the owned files; a package owns the `_test.go` of each owned source file. A compile error in a file you do
  not own is reported, not fixed.
- Order: format → lint → live check on the changed surface → scoped tests → `Skill(simplify)`; never the full suite.
- Tests: one fast regression test per bug, one end-to-end test per feature, teeth proven by breaking the fix in a copy;
  no value-pinning. A copilot test leaf writes it after the implementer returns (refactor packages get none).
- Report gross added and deleted production lines separately; a package with net growth names what it clarified.
- Write the full report to `/Users/edotau/.claude/memory/claude-code/reports/`; return at most 8 lines.
- Code leaves run on the Databricks arm (`/coworker` overlay `{"provider":"databricks","profile":"auto"}`), spread
  over dev/qa/prod; docs leaves on claude sonnet.

